```
ROLE: theory_skeptic  VOTE: yellow

MUNDANE_EXPLANATIONS:
- The "3-class win" reduces analytically to "LRU + oracle hint that ~50% of scratch is provably dead." Belady (1966) and every subsequent caching paper predicts that any policy augmented with a 'never-referenced-again' oracle dominates the same policy without the oracle. The result is FULLY PREDICTED by textbook theory; it is not an emergent or surprising finding. The 3-class machinery is wrapping paper around an oracle hint.
- The "headroom inversion fix" vs naive2 is equally mundane: naive2 was destroying COMMITTED scratch that demonstrably has temporal locality; adaptive3 stops doing that. The "fix" is "stop evicting blocks that get re-read" — not a mechanism, an undoing of a prior mistake.
- Adaptive3 - LRU Δhit grows monotonically with cap_frac (+0.5pp→+3.0pp) for the trivial reason that more headroom = more TRANSIENT blocks survive under LRU long enough to "waste" space that adaptive3 reclaims; the slope is a direct function of TRANSIENT fraction (fixed at 8/16=50%), not a property of the policy.

CONFOUNDS:
- TRANSIENT-class blocks are defined IN THE TRACE GENERATOR as "never re-referenced." The label is ground-truth by construction. In a real agentic trace a tool payload CAN be re-referenced (model quotes the tool output verbatim, retries, chained tool calls operating on prior result). Win is engineered into the trace; classifier accuracy in production is not modeled.
- The pin-shared-prefix ablation is degenerate in 19/20 cells: pin == LRU exactly (per the researcher's own disclosure), because with any headroom LRU already keeps the hot shared prefix resident. So "adaptive3 strictly Pareto-dominates pin-shared-prefix" in those 19 cells is mathematically identical to "adaptive3 beats LRU" — the ablation does not isolate what it claims to isolate. The ONE cell where pin actually does something different (cap=0.25, sf=0.90) is the cell where pin captures 99.9% of the gap — i.e. the only honest test of the ablation FAILS the empty-framing check.
- COMMITTED:TRANSIENT = 1:1 fixed at 8 blk : 8 blk. The whole effect scales with TRANSIENT fraction; sweeping this is the load-bearing sensitivity and it is NOT swept.

ASSUMPTIONS_UNTESTED:
- Perfect TRANSIENT classification at inference time. No misclassification-cost curve (what happens to hit-rate if 10%/25%/50% of TRANSIENT-labeled blocks are actually re-referenced).
- Block size (16), prefix_len (2048), turns/session (8), sessions (40), interleaved arrival pattern: single fixed configuration. No sensitivity.
- Content-addressed proxy tokens assume collision-free hashing equivalent to real vLLM block-hash semantics; not validated.
- No Belady/optimal-offline upper bound is computed. Without it we cannot tell whether adaptive3 captures 30% or 95% of the achievable headroom gain; the 1-3pp effect could be near-trivial fraction of what an oracle policy would extract.

STATISTICAL_GAPS:
- n=6 paired-bootstrap CIs are tight, but they measure simulator variance, not policy variance under real-trace heterogeneity. "CI excludes 0" on a synthetic trace where the win is mechanistically required is a low bar.
- Effect sizes are modest in the operationally interesting regime (cap≥0.5): +1.2pp..+3.0pp Δhit. The pre-registration's HELD condition requires the advantage be "a MEANINGFUL fraction of the gap to LRU" — at cap≥0.50 where pin==LRU, the "gap to LRU" IS the entire 3-class effect, so this clause is vacuously satisfied and provides no falsification power.
- The pooled "96.4% captured by pin at cap=0.25" reported in stdout is, by the researcher's own admission, dominated by a single cell (cap=0.25, sf=0.90). Pooling across shared_prefix_frac when one cell behaves qualitatively differently masks the very effect under test. Disaggregated reporting is in the packet — but the pre-registered decision rule was pooled, weakening the registration.
- naive2 marginally beats adaptive3 at cap≤0.5 (a3−naive2 = −0.0037, −0.0011). The committee's stated frame is "fix naive2's defect"; the deepest-starvation regime is the one regime where naive2 was supposedly worst, and adaptive3 LOSES there. This is in tension with the candidate-grade framing.

RATIONALE:
The result is real, pre-registered, and honestly disclosed — credit for the (cap=0.25, sf=0.90) and naive2-starvation blemishes. But the theoretical content is thin: the win is the predicted Belady-style benefit of an oracle dead-block hint, and the pin-shared-prefix ablation is degenerate (pin==LRU exactly) in 19/20 cells, so it does NOT actually rule out the "trivial shared-prefix pinning" null in the cells where it could have. YELLOW with concrete required_evidence for the GPU pass: (1) live ≥2-source prior-art sweep per VERDICT-0001 item (2) — still owed; (2) sweep COMMITTED:TRANSIENT ratio at minimum {1:3, 1:1, 3:1} — the load-bearing parameter; (3) Belady/oracle-offline upper bound on the same trace, so the reported 1-3pp gains are interpretable as a fraction of achievable headroom; (4) misclassification robustness — degradation curve when X% of TRANSIENT blocks are actually re-referenced (with X swept to where adaptive3 collapses to LRU); (5) real vLLM enable_prefix_caching on H100/devgpu014 with a two-typed agentic trace where TRANSIENT classification is derived from a real prompt-template inspector (not an oracle label), so we measure the SYSTEM (classifier + eviction), not the oracle in isolation; (6) report per-cell, not pooled, to avoid the cap=0.25 corner masking the disaggregated story. Without (3) and (4) the GPU pass would replicate a tautology at higher fidelity. green is not earned; red is not earned (the result is honest and the registration was respected); YELLOW is the calibrated vote.
```
